      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "A high-dynamic-range electron microscopy camera developed at Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory captures strong and faint signals simultaneously, generating over 500 Gbps of data that can be processed during acquisition.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/enabling-real-time-ai-for-scientific-instruments-with-gpu-native-data-acquisition/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-21T17:25:55.310Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA DAQIRI is a software-defined data acquisition library that moves high-bandwidth instrument and sensor data into GPU-ready workflows.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/enabling-real-time-ai-for-scientific-instruments-with-gpu-native-data-acquisition/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-21T17:25:55.310Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "For existing Ethernet-capable instruments, this opens opportunities to add processing and feedback capabilities, as described in the previous post, Enable Real-Time AI for High-Speed Data Acquisition with NVIDIA DAQIRI .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/enabling-real-time-ai-for-scientific-instruments-with-gpu-native-data-acquisition/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-21T17:25:55.310Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "This advancement simplifies the experimental setup and microscope optics, but generates more than 500 gigabits of data per second (Gbps)—a stream that must be received and processed to make those measurements useful during acquisition.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/enabling-real-time-ai-for-scientific-instruments-with-gpu-native-data-acquisition/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-21T17:25:55.310Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "This is over 500x faster than conventional EELS data streams, which greatly enhances the raw detector information available for further processing and analysis.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/enabling-real-time-ai-for-scientific-instruments-with-gpu-native-data-acquisition/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-21T17:25:55.310Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Through this pipeline, the team enables inspection of the data during the measurement and adjusting the acquisition parameters and regions of interest in real time, all while processing high bandwidth data incoming at more than 500 Gbps.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/enabling-real-time-ai-for-scientific-instruments-with-gpu-native-data-acquisition/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-21T17:25:55.310Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "During the process of making scientific instruments, GPU-native data acquisition enables you to design around what will be measured and your desired means of response.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/enabling-real-time-ai-for-scientific-instruments-with-gpu-native-data-acquisition/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
